      "question": "Why is chunking necessary, and how does chunk overlap help retrieval?",
      "status": "PASS",
      "answer": "Chunking is necessary because it helps to manage and process large amounts of data more efficiently. By dividing a long document into smaller pieces (chunks), it becomes easier to index, process, and understand the content.\n\nChunk overlap, in this context, helps retrieval by allowing for a more flexible and robust search. Overlapping chunks ensure that similar information is found across multiple chunks, improving the chances of retrieving relevant information during a search. This method also makes the system more resilient to missing or incomplete chunks, as the overlapping areas can compensate for any missing data.",
